WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.200
A few months ago, I went to
Zwentendorf in Austria,

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.560
which is a nuclear power
plant that was built,

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.110
and ready to go, and then cancelled.

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:10.420
And it's now a training
centre and accidental museum

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.434
because, well, what else would you do

00:00:12.434 --> 00:00:15.540
with a never-used nuclear power plant?

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:16.730
- This is Wunderland Kalkar,

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:19.300
it's a theme park opened in 2001.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.370
Each year, we get about 280,000
visitors here in the park.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:27.580
The Dutch entrepreneur Van der Most,
he bought this in 1996.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:30.260
And from that time on,
the first four or five years,

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:33.470
we just put everything out
of it and start to rebuild

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:35.950
the whole area to what it is now.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:40.460
- This was SNR-300, and its story
is much the same as Zwentendorf's

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:43.610
It was a nuclear power plant
ready to go in Germany

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.230
and then public protests
and political problems

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:49.516
meant that the whole project
was postponed for a long, long while,

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:51.600
and then Chernobyl
happened in Ukraine

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:54.150
and the tide of public opinion
changed even further,

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.890
and the whole project was just cancelled.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.230
The reactor itself, all the
valuable stuff in there,

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:01.200
well, that was sold off
for parts and for scrap,

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.650
but the land, well, that was
sold off in the nineties.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.410
- What we've got now is a theme park

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:09.730
with approximately 40 attractions.

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:11.910
Of course there's a carousel,
there's the teacups

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.170
the elephants, and
there's also a very nice

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:16.060
rollercoaster here in the park.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:17.520
One of the important things we've got

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.070
is in the cooling tower,
that's the Vertical Swing.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.130
We've got a hotel with a thousand beds,

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.940
and we've got a big exhibition hall

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:27.070
with 9,000 square metres
where you can have

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:28.880
all kinds of exhibitions.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:31.640
Two-thirds of the buildings at
the moment are still empty.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:34.750
For example, the building behind us there
was the reactor building.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.180
The reactor building,
there's nothing in it at the moment,

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:39.500
but we want to make a new landscape in it

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.590
with all kinds of wellness area,

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:44.070
but also a kind of winter landscape.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.780
- This is just a small local theme park.

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:48.670
You shouldn't expect hyper-coasters
or anything with the polish of Disney,

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:51.020
but they do have one unique ride.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.910
Not because of the ride itself,

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:55.600
that's just an off-the-shelf Star Flyer,

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.270
you can ride those a lot
of places in the world,

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:00.520
but not inside a cooling tower.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:03.053
And the view is spectacular.

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:07.150
Oh, I should not have looked down.

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:08.983
I should not have looked down.

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:16.130
Thank you so much to everyone
at Wunderland Kalkar.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:20.330
The season continues for a couple of weeks
as this video goes live, and then

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:21.930
they'll be open again next year.

